rfaces verified against each client's own `--help` / official docs, cited in the setup doc' — the observed --help/doc output is not in the plan; verification is deferred to the doc.","External CLIs (copilot/codex/claude) are not probeable from this environment; evidence class = Unverified for each per-client key/subcommand.","T3 empiricism-depth axis (a): OBSERVE flag names from --help, do not infer from memory; flag-level mismatches cause silent runtime failures.","resolve_symbol confirms only the Python `mcp` SDK exists locally, not the three client binaries — the client surfaces cannot be confirmed here."],"finding":"The three external client CLI/config surfaces the plan depends on (codex `bearer_token_env_var` under `[mcp_servers.rebar]`; copilot `type: http` + `headers` in `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` via `copilot mcp add --transport http --header`; claude `type: http` + `${VAR}` in `.mcp.json`; and the acceptance subcommands `copilot mcp get rebar` / `codex mcp list` / `claude mcp list`) are asserted as verified against each client's `--help`/docs but the observed evidence is not present in the plan — the citations live only in a setup doc to be authored during execution. Per T3 these config-key/flag-level surfaces must be treated as UNVERIFIED; a wrong key or subcommand name (e.g. --header vs --headers, or a non-existent `bearer_token_env_var`) causes a silent runtime failure after ship.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe2f2c25fdf29c78b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale (static bearer for all three; sourced from client --help) — the copilot/codex/claude bullets","norm_id":"n1b52a2ef5b7f0efb","priority":0.6365,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["codex TOML has no `bearer_token_env_var` key (or it lives at a different scope), so the committed example fails to resolve the PAT and the read-tool call 401s.","copilot's config key is not `type`/`headers` or the file is not `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json`, so `copilot mcp get rebar` does not load the committed example."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.95,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concrete basis for the structural loader's per-client schema validation (e.g. a checked-in JSON Schema per client, or the explicit set of required keys/types the loader asserts), so the hermetic oracle's validity is grounded rather than referencing an unspecified 'documented schema'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'validates it against that client's documented schema'","Client-binary acceptance checks all skip-with-reason when the CLI is absent, so in binary-less CI the structural loader is the sole shape-oracle","No source is given for the 'documented schema' the loader checks against"],"finding":"The 'client-agnostic structural loader' oracle validates each example config 'against that client's documented schema', but the plan does not state where that per-client schema comes from (a machine-readable JSON Schema? a hand-coded set of required keys?). In hermetic CI (no client binaries installed) this loader is the ONLY thing proving each config's shape is correct, so its validation basis is load-bearing yet unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6aff154a26d0734d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — Real-tool-result oracle","norm_id":"nc343460fa8b81202","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A CI runner without copilot/codex/claude binaries where the structural loader must fully substitute for real-CLI validation"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the structural loader models each client's substitution SEPARATELY — codex bearer_token_env_var as env-var name indirection, copilot $VAR and claude ${VAR} as literal expansion — and assert per-client (not one shared) resolution semantics in the always-run oracle.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'resolves the bearer via the client's documented env-var substitution'","Plan Codex bullet: 'bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\" so the PAT comes from the environment' (name indirection)","Plan Copilot bullet: 'the CLI expands $VAR from the environment'; Claude bullet: 'Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE}' (literal expansion)","The CLI acceptance checks 'skip-with-reason when the CLI is absent' so the true-client resolution is not exercised unconditionally"],"finding":"The always-run 'client-agnostic structural loader' oracle resolves the bearer via 'the client's documented env-var substitution' as if the three clients share one substitution mechanism, but they do not: codex's bearer_token_env_var is name-indirection (the client reads the named env var itself) while copilot ($VAR) and claude (${VAR}) are literal string expansions. A single loader that conflates these can validate a config the real client would resolve differently, and the only faithful oracle (the CLI-binary check) skips-with-reason in hermetic CI.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f683a7a4a58027302","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria → first bullet (Real-tool-result oracle) and Approach section (Codex bearer_token_env_var vs Copilot/Claude $VAR)","norm_id":"n5ffbca9319270eab","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A codex config whose bearer_token_env_var value is written like a copilot $VAR literal (or vice-versa) passes the shared loader but the real client resolves a different/empty bearer","CI is green because the CLI oracle skipped, masking a per-client substitution divergence"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the Claude static-header precedence/no-OAuth-fallback claim against a specific current code.claude.com/docs version, and note the known contrary behavior when the server advertises OAuth (anthropics/claude-code #59467/#80785/#82534) so the setup doc reflects actual, not assumed, client behavior.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5093,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'a static header takes precedence and does NOT fall back to OAuth if rejected, so a wrong/expired PAT fails hard (not a silent OAuth retry)'","Retrieved GitHub issue anthropics/claude-code #59467 (title: 'HTTP MCP client ignores configured Authorization header when ...'): 'when ... configured ... with a static Authorization: Bearer header AND the server also advertises OAuth ... Claude Code ignores the configured header and falls back to OAuth discovery' — the OPPOSITE of the plan's claim","Retrieved GitHub issue anthropics/claude-code #80785: client 'appears to attempt an OAuth discovery probe ... even though only a static Authorization header was configured, and fails hard when the server's response ... doesn't match ... instead of falling back to the configured header auth'","Retrieved GitHub issue anthropics/claude-code #82534: 'connectivity preflight omits configured [header] ... the connection fails even though the token is valid and correctly stored'","ABSENCE: the plan cites 'code.claude.com/docs mcp' generally but pins the precedence/no-fallback behavior to no specific doc/version; retrieved issues show it depends on whether the rebar endpoint advertises OAuth"],"finding":"The plan states as settled fact that Claude Code's static Authorization header 'takes precedence and does NOT fall back to OAuth if rejected, so a wrong/expired PAT fails hard (not a silent OAuth retry)', but this behavior is contested and appears version/server-dependent in current sources.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9db8d44b73318e3c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale → Claude bullet ('Document the gotcha: a static header takes precedence and does NOT fall back to OAuth if rejected')","norm_id":"n075a53a37f0809c5","priority":0.1907,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The rebar /mcp/ endpoint advertises OAuth as an alternative auth method: Claude may ignore the configured static header and fall back to OAuth discovery, contradicting the documented gotcha","A user's Claude Code version exhibits the preflight/OAuth-probe bug (#82534/#80785): connection fails even with a valid PAT, and the plan's setup doc would mis-advise them that a hard failure implies a bad PAT"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Cite the exact Claude Code doc section + version for the header-precedence claim, and add a caveat that if the rebar endpoint advertises OAuth metadata the CLI may attempt OAuth discovery instead of honoring the static header (per open anthropics/claude-code issues); confirm the loopback rebar-mcp used in the smoke test does NOT advertise OAuth so the 401-contrast oracle's request-path assumption holds.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the exact codex streamable-HTTP TOML key that sources a bearer from the environment (asserted `bearer_token_env_var` under `[mcp_servers.rebar]`) against codex docs/--help, and state how the client-agnostic loader models codex's env-name indirection distinctly from copilot/claude's Authorization-header substitution.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7515,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Committed template lines 15-19: `\"copilot\"/\"codex\"/\"claude\"` each `{ \"authorization\": \"Bearer REPLACE_WITH_*_PAT\" }` — a uniform header model.","Plan: codex uses `bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\"` — env-var NAME indirection, not an Authorization header, a genuinely different substitution mechanism.","Acceptance oracle already anticipates this ('resolves the bearer via the client's documented env-var substitution'), but the plan does not confirm the codex TOML key exists."],"finding":"The codex config shape diverges from the already-committed avians template without the plan reconciling the two. `mcp-clients.local.example.json` models all three clients uniformly as `\"authorization\": \"Bearer <PAT>\"`, but the plan's codex entry uses `bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\"` (env-var-NAME indirection, no Authorization header). The plan's own client-agnostic loader must therefore model codex substitution differently from copilot/claude, and that hinges on the unconfirmed `bearer_token_env_var` key existing in the codex streamable-HTTP TOML.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22574820a5a8146f","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale — Codex bullet; cross-referenced with committed mcp-clients.local.example.json","norm_id":"n3ac071c11394d6e0","priority":0.1485,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The loader assumes a uniform Authorization-header shape (matching the avians template) and mis-handles codex's env-name indirection, or the `bearer_token_env_var` key does not exist and codex silently sends no auth."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.45,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the URL scheme to https:// in all three committed example configs (Codex and Claude, not just Copilot) so no copy-ready example models a plaintext bearer transport.","cohort":["T5c"],"criteria":["T5c"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.735,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Copilot bullet says 'the HTTPS /mcp/ URL' but the Codex bullet says only 'a [mcp_servers.rebar] streamable-HTTP entry' and the Claude bullet 'type: http' names a transport type, not a URL scheme","Existing committed template already pins TLS: mcp-clients.local.example.json:14 \"url\": \"https://REPLACE_WITH_BOX_HOST/mcp/\"","Boundary: the bearer PAT crosses the public internet from client to the remote AWS box; a plaintext example URL invites an operator to copy a cleartext transport (OWASP A02 cryptographic-failure / transport)"],"finding":"The plan pins the URL scheme to HTTPS only for the Copilot example config; the Codex ('streamable-HTTP entry') and Claude ('type: http') example configs do not state an https:// scheme. A copy-ready example that models a plaintext http:// URL would transmit the client bearer PAT over cleartext to the remote box.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6612023d09dda249","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale (Codex and Claude bullets); Acceptance Criteria (committed example configs)","norm_id":"nbe107b5770a24cfa","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator copies the Codex or Claude example verbatim with an http:// (non-TLS) host and the per-client PAT is sent in the clear"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State explicitly in the Codex and Claude bullets (and the shipped examples/mcp-clients/ files) that the server URL is the HTTPS /mcp/ endpoint, matc